# Known false positives for the `secrets-scan` CI job (gitleaks).
#
# Each entry is a gitleaks Fingerprint (<commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>) --
# see https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks#gitleaksignore. gitleaks scans
# `git log -p`, i.e. each historical commit's own patch content, so a fixed
# string already committed cannot be un-flagged by editing it in a later
# commit (that only changes what the *new* commit's patch contains); this
# file is the supported way to allowlist a specific historical finding
# without rewriting git history.

